WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.

2
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.080
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

3
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.

4
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.

5
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.440
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.420
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.560
We're The Office ladies.

8
00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:25.900
It's the merger.

9
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:27.360
Hi, everyone.

10
00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:28.640
We're merging.

11
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:29.960
Where are we merging to?

12
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:37.120
We are merging two worlds today, Angela, the Stanford and the Scranton branches.

13
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:42.100
Not all of the Stanford branch, but some will be merging with Scranton.

14
00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:46.020
I also feel like we're merging as friends because I'm looking at you.

15
00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:49.040
I think we have almost the same outfit on today.

16
00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:55.380
You know, I mean, seriously, like they always say like pet owners start to look like their pets.

17
00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.700
Best friends start to look like each other and like husbands and wives and partners.

18
00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.500
Like I feel like we're starting to look like each other.

19
00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:03.960
We might be.

20
00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:08.060
Also, neither one of us has had a haircut or a hair color in a very long time.

21
00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:10.020
I did my own hair color, lady.

22
00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:11.080
I did too.

23
00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:15.680
Well, actually, Lee did mine with my hair colorist on FaceTime.

24
00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:17.900
I did mine.

25
00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:19.520
But no, I haven't had a haircut.

26
00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:22.640
And I kind of have given up on makeup.

27
00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:23.780
Just lipstick.

28
00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.320
Do you notice I only wear lipstick?

29
00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:28.340
Yeah, you show up to these Zooms in lipstick.

30
00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:34.700
I was walking out to my That's What She Said to start the Zoom and I put on a little lipstick and the kids were like, why are you putting on lipstick?

31
00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:39.660
And I was like, because I'm, yeah, because.

32
00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:43.280
Yes, I will be on a Zoom.

33
00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:44.760
I'm going to be on a Zoom.

34
00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:45.440
All right.

35
00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:53.040
Well, this is season three, episode eight, written by Brent Forrester and directed by Ken Whittingham.

36
00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.100
Do you want a summary?

37
00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:56.100
I do want a summary.

38
00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:56.840
All right.

39
00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:57.180
Good.

40
00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:05.000
The Stanford branch merges with the Scranton branch, which means Jim will be returning to his old stomping ground.

41
00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:05.620
Oh.

42
00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:06.420
Oh.

43
00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:07.600
Woo-hoo-hoo.

44
00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:09.360
Bam is so excited.

45
00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:17.280
Michael does his best to welcome the Stanford transplants, but he goes a bit too far, causing one employee to quit.

46
00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:25.840
But Michael tries to save face by then firing him, leaving Dunder Mifflin with having to pay a sizable severance.

47
00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:27.980
Jan's not happy.

48
00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.060
Jan is not happy.

49
00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:38.040
Meanwhile, Pam senses something is going on with Jim and Karen and Dwight clashes with Andy.

50
00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:40.360
Good summary, lady.

51
00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:41.200
Thanks.

52
00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:42.560
You know what I started realizing?

53
00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:43.460
What?

54
00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:46.540
You know how I have that Bible from The Office?

55
00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:47.560
The Office Bible?

56
00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:48.080
Yeah.

57
00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:48.520
Yeah.

58
00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.380
Every show has a summary.

59
00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.980
Every episode has a summary in The Office Bible.

60
00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:57.600
So I've been able to now refer to The Office Bible summary.

61
00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:58.920
I tweak it a little.

62
00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:00.560
I put a little zhuzh on it.

63
00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:06.420
But yeah, I used to just sit down at a blank page and think, how do I summarize this episode?

64
00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:12.160
And a team of writers have done it for me, and it was just sitting on my desk.

65
00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:17.140
So if you've noticed my summaries are getting better, it's thanks to The Office Bible.

66
00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:18.300
Wow.

67
00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:22.540
How excited were you when you realized there were summaries in there?

68
00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.120
You must have been so excited.

69
00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:25.720
Lady, yes.

70
00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:26.640
So excited.

71
00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:30.780
Fast fact number one, this episode was directed by Ken Whittingham.

72
00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:32.820
We've talked a little bit about Ken before.

73
00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:38.140
Ken directed nine episodes of The Office, including this one.

74
00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:40.240
And we reached out to him.

75
00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.040
Yes, and he sent in some audio clips.

76
00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:45.620
We're really excited to hear him talk about this episode.

77
00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:51.740
And Jenna, he is going to come on and be a full Zoom guest for Phyllis's wedding.

78
00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.020
I don't want to get ahead of ourselves, but we're very excited.

79
00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:58.440
Yes, and Phyllis's wedding is such a milestone episode, and so is this.

80
00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:03.880
We wanted to ask, Ken, what was it like to merge these two worlds?

81
00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:06.660
And a lot of people wrote in wanting to know,

82
00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:10.440
how did they decide where everybody would sit in the office?

83
00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:15.180
Like, if you notice, suddenly the desk pods go from two to three.

84
00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:16.140
Yeah.

85
00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:19.820
I remember being so happy that Ken was the one directing this,

86
00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.420
because we already knew Ken really well.

87
00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:22.720
We were so comfortable with him.

88
00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.160
And this was big even for the cast, Jenna.

89
00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:28.940
There was a buzz, because we hadn't been around these people.

90
00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:33.400
And, you know, we barely got to see them at table reads and things like that.

91
00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:38.540
So there was a real sort of buzz on set, and I remember being happy that Ken was there,

92
00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:42.580
because he's so calm and, like, that he was going to guide us through the merger.

93
00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:50.840
Well, here is his audio clip explaining how he and Greg decided where all the new people would sit.

94
00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:55.980
Introducing the characters from the Stanford branch would be very important to establish these characters

95
00:04:55.980 --> 00:05:00.220
and how they interacted with the Scranton employees, their likes and their dislikes for each other.

96
00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:05.220
I remember Greg Daniels asking me to decide where the new characters would sit and why.

97
00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:08.980
So he and I walked to the set, and I laid out where I thought everyone should be.

98
00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:14.160
Since Ryan had taken Jim's old desk, I decided that Jim would sit directly across from Dwight,

99
00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:16.700
which would be fun for Jim and irritating to Dwight.

100
00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:22.280
It would also put Jim in the middle of Karen and Pam, which would also make Jim uncomfortable,

101
00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:25.900
and Pam to be able to check out interactions between him and Karen.

102
00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:31.700
I set Andy in between Kevin and Angela to establish Andy's instant attraction to Angela,

103
00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:35.580
and also they would be in Dwight's eyeline to create Dwight's jealousy.

104
00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:38.640
Andy would later move on to Karen's desk.

105
00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:46.120
I placed Tony in the back near Toby at a very obscure desk because he would be quitting or getting fired in that episode.

106
00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:53.060
We also discussed how important it was to build Pam's awareness that Jim had moved on and was interested in Karen.

107
00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:58.200
I love how much thought went into where everyone sat.

108
00:05:58.540 --> 00:05:59.620
I love it so much.

109
00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:04.860
I love the idea of, depending on which character, who could see who, right?

110
00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:05.360
Yes.

111
00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:06.080
Yeah.

112
00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:10.620
And thinking about it from Pam's perspective, and I remember sitting at the desk,

113
00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:15.900
and there's even a moment in the episode when Pam realizes she's not going to be able to see Jim's face anymore.

114
00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:16.560
Yeah.

115
00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:21.260
There's a whole deleted scene about that, lady, where you actually come up to him,

116
00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:22.400
and you're like, this is kind of weird.

117
00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:24.100
I just stare at your back now.

118
00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:25.620
It's, really?

119
00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:25.670
Yeah.

120
00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:27.300
It's a great deleted scene.

121
00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:31.700
And you and Jim start doing a bit, and then Ryan's like, can you guys stop?

122
00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.160
I'm just trying to get some work done.

123
00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:34.600
It's really awkward.

124
00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:35.160
Oh, my gosh.

125
00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:36.740
I want to go back and see that.

126
00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:37.340
Yeah.

127
00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:44.780
Because also, after I heard Ken's clip, I was thinking about how, wow, so now Pam can see Karen's face.

128
00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:52.780
So if Karen is making flirty googly eyes at Jim or something, she doesn't know if Jim is reciprocating or not,

129
00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:54.700
because she can only see the back of his head.

130
00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:55.500
Yeah.

131
00:06:55.960 --> 00:07:03.240
So in terms of Pam trying to track this relationship going forward, she's only going to have that one thing she can see.

132
00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:08.800
It's just, I just love, I love all the thought that goes into these choices.

133
00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:09.960
Yes.

134
00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:15.620
And some people I saw wrote in and asked, why would Andy sit in Oscar's desk and where is Oscar?

135
00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:18.920
But you have to remember, Oscar is on his paid vacation leave.

136
00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:19.500
Yeah.

137
00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:20.920
So his desk was available.

138
00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:21.700
Yeah.

139
00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:29.300
Although, I will say this, Angela, someone wrote in to note that the character of Hannah is technically an accountant.

140
00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:31.000
Oh.

141
00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:31.840
Yeah.

142
00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:32.640
So maybe.

143
00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:35.900
Maybe that's another layer why my character feels so threatened by her.

144
00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:36.500
Yeah.

145
00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:37.300
Exactly.

146
00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:39.280
There can only be one bitch in accounting.

147
00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:41.700
All right.

148
00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:42.780
Well, I loved that.

149
00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:45.340
Let's move on to fastback number two.

150
00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:49.660
This is the first episode featuring writer Brent Forrester.

151
00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:50.980
Yes.

152
00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:54.220
And Brent also sent in audio clips.

153
00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:57.560
We asked him a lot of questions and he sent in clips as well.

154
00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:03.760
So all throughout this episode, you guys, we're going to have clips from Ken, the director, and Brent, the writer, which is just so fun.

155
00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:04.340
Yeah.

156
00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:06.400
I love getting to have those different perspectives.

157
00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:13.680
So Angela, you asked Brent about what it was like for him to write his first episode.

158
00:08:13.980 --> 00:08:14.420
Yeah.

159
00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:17.540
This was his first episode and it's such a huge one.

160
00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:19.820
I was like, Brent, that feels very intimidating.

161
00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:23.080
You know, you're writing the merger of Scranton and Stanford.

162
00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:24.180
What was that like?

163
00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:24.600
Yeah.

164
00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:26.380
And this is what he had to say.

165
00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:30.440
Hi, I'm Brent Forrester, the author of The Merger.

166
00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:33.960
I was not part of the original writing staff of The Office.

167
00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:41.080
Greg Daniels, the show creator, was a writer with me on The Simpsons and he had me as a writer on King of the Hill.

168
00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:43.120
He brought me in in season three.

169
00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:52.020
And what I remember most about writing this draft was how I totally failed in the first draft to capture the tone of The Office.

170
00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:54.300
I was trying so hard to be funny.

171
00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:58.660
I wrote witticisms for every character in The Office every time they opened their mouth.

172
00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:00.480
And Greg was so horrified.

173
00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:09.820
He made Mike Schur, Jen Salata, and Paul Lieberstein, the three senior writers on the show, sit me down and explain to me the tone of The Office,

174
00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:17.420
which is the tone of naturalism, where we don't require characters to be saying funny things all the time,

175
00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:23.700
where we let things be dramatic for long stretches, and where we get comedy from performance above all.

176
00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:37.020
Well, I transformed as a writer between draft one and two of The Merger, and I learned the tone of The Office real faSt.

177
00:09:37.940 --> 00:09:38.780
Oh, Brent.

178
00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:39.480
Don't you love that?

179
00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:41.880
I just love that he was like, yeah, I got it wrong.

180
00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:47.260
They kind of like let me know what was what, and then I gave it another try.

181
00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:53.180
Well, what people should know is that Brent went on to be a co-executive producer of The Office.

182
00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:57.420
He ended up running the show with Paul Lieberstein, so he figured it out.

183
00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:58.640
He figured it out.

184
00:09:58.720 --> 00:09:59.820
Yeah, he did just fine.

185
00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:00.700
That's right.

186
00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:01.760
Okay, I'm so excited.

187
00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:04.300
We're going to have more clips from him coming up, too.

188
00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:04.880
Yeah.

189
00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:10.440
Fast fact number three, let's talk about the transfers from Stanford.

190
00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:12.720
Yes, Stanford.

191
00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:15.420
Here are our new characters.

192
00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:19.300
We have Tony Gardner, played by Mike Bruner.

193
00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:28.500
We have Ursula Burton, who plays Hannah, and we have Wayne Wilderson, who plays Martin Nash.

194
00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:35.360
Now, you might recognize Mike Bruner because he did have a small scene with Rashida in an earlier episode.

195
00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:39.380
Hannah was in the background of a few scenes over in Stanford.

196
00:10:39.380 --> 00:10:44.480
She had this storyline and some deleted scenes with Jim, but they had been cut.

197
00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:50.700
And then you might recognize Wayne because he had a big recurring role on Veep.

198
00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:53.420
And by the way, now he's in Greg's new show, Upload.

199
00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:54.800
Nice.

200
00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:55.100
Nice.

201
00:10:55.500 --> 00:11:00.740
And I want to take a tangent real quickly, Angela, to say that I'm really loving Upload.

202
00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:09.080
It is, I know it's like sci-fi-y, but I'm super digging it because I realized something about my sci-fi thing.

203
00:11:09.340 --> 00:11:09.820
What?

204
00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:19.340
Okay, I really like Black Mirror as well, and I feel like Upload has a type of sort of a comedic Black Mirror thing going on.

205
00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:21.880
And is that sci-fi?

206
00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:24.600
Is Black Mirror sci-fi fantasy?

207
00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:27.200
Yeah, I would say it is.

208
00:11:27.340 --> 00:11:32.900
It's a lot of like alternate realities and sort of, yeah, it is.

209
00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:33.680
I think it is.

210
00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:38.420
Okay, is Handmaid's Tale sci-fi fantasy?

211
00:11:39.140 --> 00:11:40.120
See what I'm saying?

212
00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:42.900
This is the category that I like.

213
00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:45.480
I like a tiny spin.

214
00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:47.300
I love zombie movies.

215
00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:48.680
I love a tiny...

216
00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:50.460
I feel like zombie is horror, though.

217
00:11:50.800 --> 00:12:02.360
I know, but I feel like it's falling in this new category that I want to designate, which is like, it's some of life as we know it and then some new rules.

218
00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:04.380
Slightly altered reality.

219
00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:05.940
Altered reality.

220
00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:08.640
I'm doing a lot of gestures right now.

221
00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:09.120
You are.

222
00:12:09.280 --> 00:12:10.200
I wish you could see Jenna.

223
00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:15.080
She's like cupping the air and then like spinning it over her head like it's a world, a ball.

224
00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:16.100
I don't know what's happening.

225
00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:19.660
Right, because this is reality, and then this is altered reality.

226
00:12:20.060 --> 00:12:21.000
Here's the thing, Jenna.

227
00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:22.940
Handmaid's Tale, I don't think you can handle it.

228
00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:23.680
I watched it.

229
00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:24.580
It's fantastic.

230
00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:25.880
I couldn't sleep at night.

231
00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:26.820
I was like, oh my gosh.

232
00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:32.120
I watched one episode of Handmaid's Tale, and I had nightmares for three nights.

233
00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:32.740
Oh, yeah.

234
00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:33.520
Oh, yeah.

235
00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:38.220
And I've seen a lot of horror films, but that was, I mean, that got in my head.

236
00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:39.320
Holy moly.

237
00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:40.180
Okay, so.

238
00:12:40.180 --> 00:12:41.560
But here's what I'm saying.

239
00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:45.540
I feel like there is a tangent.

240
00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:47.580
Here's what I will not let go.

241
00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:53.100
I think there's a tangent of sci-fi that I'm super into, and it's altered reality sci-fi.

242
00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:56.800
